⚙️ How It Works
The Hospital Management System is designed to manage Appointments, Patients, Doctors, and Medical Records inside Salesforce. Here’s the workflow:

Appointment Creation

Receptionists create an Appointment record (Appointment__c) for a Patient (Contact).

Each Appointment is linked to both a Doctor and a Patient via lookup fields.

Appointment type can be In‑Person Visit or Telemedicine, controlled by Record Types.

Medical Records

Each Appointment can have multiple Medical Records (Medical_Record__c) attached.

Medical Records are in a Master‑Detail relationship with Appointment, so deleting an Appointment deletes its Medical Records.

Records store diagnosis, prescriptions, vitals, and follow‑up date.

Automation

Formula Fields calculate Days Since Appointment, Is Overdue, and Appointment Summary.

Roll‑Up Summary Fields show total Medical Records and finalized ones directly on the Appointment.

Validation Rules enforce business logic (e.g., no past scheduling, completed appointments must have a date).

Flows automate:

Auto‑set Priority to High for Cardiology/Neurology.

Create a follow‑up Task for the Doctor when an Appointment is marked Completed.

Copy Patient Blood Type into Appointment when created.

Screen Flow allows Receptionists to book appointments directly from the Patient’s Contact page.

Security & Access

Profiles control permissions:

Doctors can read/create/edit but not delete.

Receptionists can manage appointments but not medical records.

Field‑Level Security hides Consultation Fee from Doctors.

OWD & Role Hierarchy ensure appointments are private by default, with access flowing upward to managers.

Sharing Rules open access selectively (e.g., High Priority appointments shared with Emergency Team).

Data Quality

Matching & Duplicate Rules prevent duplicate patient records.

Validation Rules enforce consistency in appointment scheduling and status changes.

🧩 End‑to‑End Flow
Receptionist books an appointment via Quick Action Flow on the Patient’s Contact.

Appointment record is created, linked to Doctor and Patient.

Medical Records are added under the Appointment.

Automations keep data consistent (priority, overdue checks, roll‑ups).

Security ensures only the right people see/edit the right data.

Managers and emergency teams get access through role hierarchy and sharing rules.

